{"1-9":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"G1154","lemma":"Δαμασκός","tr":"Damaskos","gloss":"Damascus","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":15},{"base":"G4549","lemma":"Σαούλ","tr":"Saoul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"G4569","lemma":"Σαῦλος","tr":"Saulos","gloss":"Saul","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"G1377","lemma":"διώκω","tr":"diōkō","gloss":"to pursue","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":45},{"base":"G5101","lemma":"τίς","tr":"tis","gloss":"which?","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":557},{"base":"G0991","lemma":"βλέπω","tr":"blepō","gloss":"to see","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":132},{"base":"G5456","lemma":"φωνή","tr":"phōnē","gloss":"voice","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":139},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"G0435","lemma":"ἀνήρ","tr":"anēr","gloss":"man","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":216},{"base":"G1093","lemma":"γῆ","tr":"gē","gloss":"earth: planet","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":248}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":8,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"But Saul began to destroy the church. Going from house to house, he dragged off men and women and put them in prison.","from":1},{"book":"1TI","chapter":1,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"I was formerly a blasphemer, a persecutor, and a violent man; yet because I had acted in ignorance and unbelief, I was shown mercy.","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"My companions saw the light, but they could not understand the voice of the One speaking to me.","from":7},{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Because the brilliance of the light had blinded me, my companions led me by the hand into Damascus.","from":8},{"book":"GAL","chapter":1,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"For you have heard of my former way of life in Judaism, how severely I persecuted the church of God and tried to destroy it.","from":1},{"book":"DAN","chapter":10,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Only I, Daniel, saw the vision; the men with me did not see it, but a great terror fell upon them, and they ran and hid themselves.","from":7},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But when some of them stubbornly refused to believe and publicly maligned the Way, Paul took his disciples and left the synagogue to conduct daily discussions in the lecture hall of Tyrannus.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"About that time there arose a great disturbance about the Way.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"10-19":{"people":[{"id":"ananias-g0367h","name":"Ananias","kind":"person","brief":"Church prophet","count":4,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"judas-g2455l","name":"Judas","kind":"person","brief":"Christian in Damascus","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"places":[{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"straight-g2117","name":"Straight","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"tarsus-g5019","name":"Tarsus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"G0367","lemma":"Ἀνανίας","tr":"Ananias","gloss":"Ananias","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":11},{"base":"G3686","lemma":"ὄνομα","tr":"onoma","gloss":"name","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":229},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":714},{"base":"G0308","lemma":"ἀναβλέπω","tr":"anablepō","gloss":"to look up","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":25},{"base":"G3705","lemma":"ὅραμα","tr":"horama","gloss":"vision","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":215},{"base":"G2036","lemma":"εἶπον","tr":"eipon","gloss":"to say","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":926},{"base":"G1154","lemma":"Δαμασκός","tr":"Damaskos","gloss":"Damascus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"G2007","lemma":"ἐπιτίθημι","tr":"epitithēmi","gloss":"to put","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"G3704","lemma":"ὅπως","tr":"hopōs","gloss":"that","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":53}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GAL","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"But when God, who set me apart from my motherʼs womb and called me by His grace, was pleased","from":15},{"book":"GAL","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"to reveal His Son in me so that I might preach Him among the Gentiles, I did not rush to consult with flesh and blood,","from":15},{"book":"EPH","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"I became a servant of this gospel by the gift of Godʼs grace, given me through the working of His power.","from":15},{"book":"EPH","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"Though I am less than the least of all the saints, this grace was given me: to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ,","from":15},{"book":"1TH","chapter":3,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"so that none of you would be shaken by these trials. For you know that we are destined for this.","from":16},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"At my first defense, no one stood with me, but everyone deserted me. May it not be charged against them.","from":15},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, so that through me the message would be fully proclaimed, and all the Gentiles would hear it. So I was delivered from the mouth of the lion.","from":15},{"book":"ACT","chapter":21,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Coming over to us, he took Paulʼs belt, bound his own feet and hands, and said, “The Holy Spirit says: ‘In this way the Jews of Jerusalem will bind the owner of this belt and hand him over to the Gentiles.’”","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"20-25":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":22}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22}],"words":[{"base":"G4569","lemma":"Σαῦλος","tr":"Saulos","gloss":"Saul","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"G0337","lemma":"ἀναιρέω","tr":"anaireō","gloss":"to kill","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"G3571","lemma":"νύξ","tr":"nux","gloss":"night","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":61},{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":194},{"base":"G2250","lemma":"ἡμέρα","tr":"hēmera","gloss":"day","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":389},{"base":"G4199","lemma":"πορθέω","tr":"portheō","gloss":"to lay waste","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1917","lemma":"ἐπιβουλή","tr":"epiboulē","gloss":"plot","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2524","lemma":"καθίημι","tr":"kathiēmi","gloss":"to lower","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G4823","lemma":"συμβουλεύω","tr":"sumbouleuō","gloss":"to consult","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G4711","lemma":"σπυρίς","tr":"spuris","gloss":"basket","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.","from":22},{"book":"2CO","chapter":11,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"In Damascus, the governor under King Aretas secured the city of the Damascenes in order to arrest me.","from":24},{"book":"JOS","chapter":2,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then Rahab let them down by a rope through the window, since the house where she lived was built into the wall of the city.","from":25},{"book":"JHN","chapter":20,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Thomas replied, “My Lord and my God!”","from":20},{"book":"2CO","chapter":11,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"But I was lowered in a basket through a window in the wall and escaped his grasp.","from":25},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He gives power to the faint and increases the strength of the weak.","from":22},{"book":"LUK","chapter":21,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"For I will give you speech and wisdom that none of your adversaries will be able to resist or contradict.","from":22},{"book":"ACT","chapter":8,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But Saul began to destroy the church. Going from house to house, he dragged off men and women and put them in prison.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"26-31":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"barnabas-g0921g","name":"Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mary","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"greece-h3120h","name":"Greece","kind":"place","brief":"In Greece","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"caesarea-g2542h","name":"Caesarea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"tarsus-g5019","name":"Tarsus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"galilee-h1551","name":"Galilee","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"judea-h3063n","name":"Judea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":31}],"words":[{"base":"G3955","lemma":"παρρησιάζομαι","tr":"parrēsiazomai","gloss":"to preach boldly","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"G2419","lemma":"Ἱερουσαλήμ","tr":"Hierousalēm","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":77},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":714},{"base":"G4459","lemma":"πῶς","tr":"pōs","gloss":"how?!","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":103},{"base":"G3686","lemma":"ὄνομα","tr":"onoma","gloss":"name","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":229},{"base":"G3101","lemma":"μαθητής","tr":"mathētēs","gloss":"disciple","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":261},{"base":"G2980","lemma":"λαλέω","tr":"laleō","gloss":"to speak","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":294},{"base":"G1675","lemma":"Ἑλληνιστής","tr":"Hellēnistēs","gloss":"Hellenist","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2021","lemma":"ἐπιχειρέω","tr":"epicheireō","gloss":"to attempt","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G5019","lemma":"Ταρσός","tr":"Tarsos","gloss":"Tarsus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":111,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom; all who follow His precepts gain rich understanding. His praise endures forever!","from":31},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"And I will ask the Father, and He will give you another Advocate to be with you forever—","from":31},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"I will not leave you as orphans; I will come to you.","from":31},{"book":"ISA","chapter":33,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"He will be the sure foundation for your times, a storehouse of salvation, wisdom, and knowledge. The fear of the LORD is Zionʼs treasure.","from":31},{"book":"ACT","chapter":4,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Joseph, a Levite from Cyprus, whom the apostles called Barnabas (meaning Son of Encouragement),","from":27},{"book":"ACT","chapter":26,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"First to those in Damascus and Jerusalem, then to everyone in the region of Judea, and then to the Gentiles, I declared that they should repent and turn to God, performing deeds worthy of their repentance.","from":26},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"He who fears the LORD is secure in confidence, and his children shall have a place of refuge.","from":31},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life, turning a man from the snares of death.","from":31}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"32-35":{"people":[{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"aeneas-g0132","name":"Aeneas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":34}],"places":[{"id":"lod-h3850","name":"Lod","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"sharon-h8289i","name":"Sharon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":35}],"words":[{"base":"G0132","lemma":"Αἰνέας","tr":"Aineas","gloss":"Aeneas","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G3069","lemma":"Λύδδα","tr":"Ludda","gloss":"Lydda","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"G2730","lemma":"κατοικέω","tr":"katoikeō","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":44},{"base":"G0450","lemma":"ἀνίστημι","tr":"anistēmi","gloss":"to arise","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":107},{"base":"G4074","lemma":"Πέτρος","tr":"Petros","gloss":"Peter","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":155},{"base":"G3886","lemma":"παραλύω","tr":"paraluō","gloss":"to paralyze","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G4766","lemma":"στρώννυμι","tr":"strōnnumi","gloss":"to spread","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G3638","lemma":"ὀκτώ","tr":"oktō","gloss":"eight","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G2895","lemma":"κράββατος","tr":"krabbatos","gloss":"bed","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"G2621","lemma":"κατάκειμαι","tr":"katakeimai","gloss":"to recline","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":12}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":11,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The hand of the Lord was with them, and a great number of people believed and turned to the Lord.","from":35},{"book":"MAT","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins...” Then He said to the paralytic, “Get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”","from":34},{"book":"ACT","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But Peter said, “Silver or gold I do not have, but what I have I give you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!”","from":34},{"book":"ACT","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And when Peter saw this, he addressed the people: “Men of Israel, why are you surprised by this? Why do you stare at us as if by our own power or godliness we had made this man walk?","from":34},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They lived in Gilead, in Bashan and its towns, and throughout the pasturelands of Sharon.","from":35},{"book":"ACT","chapter":9,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This became known all over Joppa, and many people believed in the Lord.","from":35},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"She continued this for many days. Eventually Paul grew so aggravated that he turned and said to the spirit, “In the name of Jesus Christ I command you to come out of her!” And the spirit left her at that very moment.","from":34},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When you are in distress and all these things have happened to you, then in later days you will return to the LORD your God and listen to His voice.","from":35}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"john-baptist-circle","title":"John the Baptist's Circle","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"36-43":{"people":[{"id":"tabitha-g5000","name":"Tabitha","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"simon-g4613n","name":"Simon","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":43}],"places":[{"id":"joppa-h3305","name":"Joppa","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"lod-h3850","name":"Lod","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":38}],"words":[{"base":"G2445","lemma":"Ἰόππη","tr":"Ioppē","gloss":"Joppa","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":10},{"base":"G4074","lemma":"Πέτρος","tr":"Petros","gloss":"Peter","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":155},{"base":"G1393","lemma":"Δορκάς","tr":"Dorkas","gloss":"Dorcas","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G5000","lemma":"Ταβιθά","tr":"Tabitha","gloss":"Tabitha","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G5253","lemma":"ὑπερῷον","tr":"huperōon","gloss":"upper room","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"G0450","lemma":"ἀνίστημι","tr":"anistēmi","gloss":"to arise","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":107},{"base":"G5503","lemma":"χήρα","tr":"chēra","gloss":"widow","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":26},{"base":"G3936","lemma":"παρίστημι","tr":"paristēmi","gloss":"to stand by","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":41},{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G5087","lemma":"τίθημι","tr":"tithēmi","gloss":"to place","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":100}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"TIT","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"This saying is trustworthy. And I want you to emphasize these things, so that those who have believed God will take care to devote themselves to good deeds. These things are excellent and profitable for the people.","from":36},{"book":"2CH","chapter":2,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"We will cut logs from Lebanon, as many as you need, and we will float them to you as rafts by sea down to Joppa. Then you can take them up to Jerusalem.”","from":36},{"book":"MAT","chapter":9,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"After the crowd had been put outside, Jesus went in and took the girl by the hand, and she got up.","from":40},{"book":"TIT","chapter":2,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"In everything, show yourself to be an example by doing good works. In your teaching show integrity, dignity,","from":36},{"book":"ACT","chapter":10,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He is staying with Simon the tanner, whose house is by the sea.”","from":43},{"book":"HEB","chapter":13,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"equip you with every good thing to do His will. And may He accomplish in us what is pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ, to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.","from":36},{"book":"EZR","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They gave money to the masons and carpenters, and food and drink and oil to the people of Sidon and Tyre to bring cedar logs from Lebanon to Joppa by sea, as authorized by Cyrus king of Persia.","from":36},{"book":"MRK","chapter":5,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And they laughed at Him. After He had put them all outside, He took the childʼs father and mother and His own companions, and went in to see the child.","from":40}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]}}